    "blog_intro": "Short guides to choosing equipment and planning your work.",
    "article_1_intro": "Start with the work you need to do. Then choose the equipment.",
    "article_1_h1": "Your fields and crops",
    "article_1_p1": "Assess the area, field shape, terrain and access roads. Open fields, vineyards and orchards need different planning. Workload is about more than hectares alone.",
    "article_1_h2": "The complete workflow",
    "article_1_p2": "Plan charging, water supply, transport and staffing alongside the drone. The number of batteries and chargers should match your actual working schedule.",
    "article_1_h3": "Service and parts",
    "article_1_p3": "Before buying, establish how you will receive technical support, which parts are available and what the training covers. Compare the cost of the complete package and its operation.",
    "article_1_h4": "A practical demonstration",
    "article_1_p4": "Describe your crops, acreage and tasks during the consultation. Request an offer suited to your conditions and verify the drone's capabilities in the manufacturer's documentation.",
    "article_2_intro": "Training, technical checks and planning your work.",
    "article_2_h1": "Know your equipment",
    "article_2_p1": "Complete practical training for your model and read the manufacturer's manual. Learn the operating modes, warnings and procedures for stopping a flight before you begin.",
    "article_2_h2": "Check the drone",
    "article_2_p2": "Follow the manufacturer's checklist to inspect the frame, propellers, batteries and spraying system. Do not start a flight with faulty equipment or unresolved warnings.",
    "article_2_h3": "Inspect the work site",
    "article_2_p3": "Identify obstacles, power lines and areas where people may be present. Assess the weather and whether the work fits the manufacturer's limits and applicable requirements.",
    "article_2_h4": "Plan the treatment",
    "article_2_p4": "Choose the product and application rate with an agronomist and according to the product label. During training, check operating parameters against the manufacturer's instructions. This guide does not replace practical training.",
